body:
@Scottmitch - no problem, it happens to all of us :).

I have made the necessary changes for 1. above (although I've followed the way it was done for HTTP such that if `validateHeaders` is set to `true` (default), header names **and** values will be validated)

Do we really need to add a `boolean convertHeaderNamesToLowerCase` to `SpdyHttpEncoder`? We don't do this for HTTP to HTTP/2 conversion (see [here](https://github.com/netty/netty/blob/master/codec-http2/src/main/java/io/netty/handler/codec/http2/HttpConversionUtil.java#L318)).  I think we should just do the same. What do you think?
